Recommended Options:
--------------------
1. MIT License (Recommended for maximum adoption)
   - Matches core dependencies: faster-whisper (MIT), demucs (MIT), audio-separator (MIT),
     original TransNetV2 (MIT).
   - Note: OpenTimelineIO and RapidOCR are Apache-2.0; WhisperX is BSD-2-Clause;
     PySceneDetect is BSD-3-Clause; Librosa is ISC. All are permissive and compatible with MIT.
   - Warning: FFmpeg binaries compiled with `--enable-gpl` (e.g. libx264) are invoked as
     external subprocesses via CLI (`ffmpeg ...`), which does not infect Python source code
     under standard OS process boundaries, provided you do not distribute GPL-compiled FFmpeg
     binaries inside your package.

2. Apache License 2.0
   - Provides explicit patent grant alongside permissive redistribution.

